WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:00.640
Dazai Osamu published <i>Run, Melos!</i> in 1940.

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.730
<b>Host
Sakai Masato</b>

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.400
At the time,

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.900
Dazai had married Ishihara Michiko

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:09.070
Married Ishihara Michiko

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.690
after they were brought together by Ibuse Masuji.
Married Ishihara Michiko

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.450
They even had children.
Married Ishihara Michiko

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:16.370
It's said to be the most stable period in his life.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.870
Right after the marriage,

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:24.250
Dazai spoke of his determination as a writer in a letter addressed to Ibuse.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.840
"I will surely become a good writer too.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.840
I will do my job. I will not play around.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:36.140
I shall do my best to make the world just a bit brighter."

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:42.060
Dazai's firm determination had a
great influence even on his works.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.770
The style differs from books he later wrote like <i>No Longer Human</i>.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.560
Starting with <i>Run, Melos!</i>,

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.730
his works from this period were bright and kind.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.610
Bright

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.150
Kind

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:53.610
Bright

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.200
The masterpieces are blue.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.950
The
masterpieces
are blue

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.580
This is the last episode of <i>Run, Melos!</i>

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:19.350
Run, Melos!

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.020
I thought I had been deceived by Melos.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.860
He was so ridiculously simple.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.400
He was so utterly reckless.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.400
He wanted to be connected with people.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.240
He thought that everything was in his hands.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.780
Everyone is like that when they're young.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.620
But the older you get, the duller you become.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:50.630
Both hope and passion slip through your fingers like overflowing sand,

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:55.460
and a new vast gap of darkness stretches out before your eyes.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.090
People are all alone.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:29.040
Oh, Zeus!

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.880
Calm this raging stream!

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.050
If I cannot make it to the royal castle before the sun sinks,

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.300
my good friend will die for me!

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.270
But I have no better option than to jump right now!

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.060
May heaven be my witness.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.320
The great power of love and sincerity shall not lose to this muddy stream!

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:04.330
Melos jumped into the stream with a splash

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:09.040
and started a frantic struggle in
the squirming and raging stream.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.500
He slashed his way through the
surging stream with all his might.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.920
Even the gods might have been moved to pity the shape of this blind, furious child.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:24.760
Melos finally managed to reach the opposite shore.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.230
Wait!

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.440
What do you want?

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.780
I must get to the royal castle before the sun sinks.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.700
Give us all you possess.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.120
I possess nothing besides life.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.950
And even this life, my only one, shall be given to the king.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.710
We want your life.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.290
Are they following the king's orders?

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.440
I am sorry, but it is for the sake of justice.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.290
Selinuntius was...

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.220
Melos, do you know?

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:50.560
Do you know how Selinuntius feels as he waits for you?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.440
Now he could not even advance like a caterpillar.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.150
He slumped upon the grassland of the roadside.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.320
"I don't care anymore."

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.320
This sulky temper unfitting of a
hero haunted a corner of his heart.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:14.290
The true hero, Melos, is now miserable,
exhausted and unable to move from here.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.040
Your loving friend trusted you,

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:21.090
and now he shall be killed!

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.710
Traitor...

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.550
Traitor!

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:33.100
I ran until I was unable to move.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.730
Not even a single part of me
thought about breaking the promise.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:42.860
If I could, I would cut my chest
open and show my crimson heart.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:47.700
I want to show the heart through which runs blood of only love and sincerity.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:52.660
But, at this most vital moment, I have run out of both spirit and persistence.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.620
I don't care anymore.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.120
Maybe this is my fate.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.590
Forgive me, Selinuntius.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:04.630
You have always trusted me.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.010
I have never deceived you either.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.180
The two of us were very good friends!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:16.020
The dark cloud of doubt has never dwelt in our hearts.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:19.770
Even now, you must be innocently waiting for me.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.480
Waiting for me!

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.980
Thank you, Selinuntius.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.110
For trusting me.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.240
I can't even bear the thought.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:34.240
The sincerity between two friends is the proudest treasure in this world!

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.500
You'll write and I'll perform it.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:44.300
Selinuntius, I've been running.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.420
I had no intention to betray you.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.760
Trust me!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:29.880
Lies!

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.330
Takada!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.330
I'm really sorry for calling at night.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.170
How is the manuscript coming along?

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:12.220
Yesterday was the deadline, and since
you usually hand it in around this time...

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.560
Hello?

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.270
Melos won't come.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.060
Huh?

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.520
Melos will not come.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.270
Huh?

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.650
Um...

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:28.520
Ah, I get it.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.400
He won't come!
You always...

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.320
Because he didn't come either!

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.520
I told you, Takada.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:11.030
Don't waste manuscripts.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:11.480
Run, Melos!
Don't waste manuscripts.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.990
Run, Melos!

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.290
So what happens next?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.050
You haven't written it yet?

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.340
Hey, can you hear me?

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.010
I can't write!

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.270
Thanks to you!

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.600
Thanks to me?

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.560
Yes, yes!

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.480
It's your fault!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.810
Why?

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.690
Why didn't you come back then?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.780
We made a promise...

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.320
Didn't we make a promise?

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.780
We were friends.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.830
I trusted...

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.000
I trusted you...

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:10.420
I valued that promise more than I valued my life...

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.800
Take this.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:21.970
I swear that I'll be there.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:23.100
Wait for me.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.110
"Let's go to Tokyo together!"

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.820
We made that promise...

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.660
Didn't we make it?

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.910
We made a promise...

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:49.670
Just write.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.040
Keep writing till the end.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.090
I'm looking forward to it.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.670
I don't want to!

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.170
I'll wait.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.760
I'll be waiting.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.570
<i>Mister Takada.</i>

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:01.530
<i>Please forgive me for contacting you like this.</i>

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:04.570
<i>I found out your address from your publisher.</i>

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.490
<i>I'm Joshima's wife.</i>

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.540
<i>My husband has fallen ill with a heart disease,</i>

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:11.370
<i>And doesn't have much longer to live.</i>

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:15.000
<i>He said he wanted to see you for the last time.</i>

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:19.960
<i>Would you mind granting his last wish?</i>

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:27.010
Joshima's going to die?

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:33.850
Hey!

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:50.370
Melos woke up to the sound of water.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.750
He rose unsteadily,

00:12:52.750 --> 00:13:00.090
looked and saw spring water gushing
forth copiously from a crack in a rock.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.310
I can walk.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.560
I shall go.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:15.730
I shall go.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.110
There is still time left before the sunset.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:20.980
There is a person waiting for me!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.440
He trusts me.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.700
My life does not matter.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.910
I must reward his faith.

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:36.420
That's all I can do now!

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.210
Run, Melos!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:46.970
Faster!

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:49.090
Faster!

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:53.970
Much faster!

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:08.610
He pushed people away and knocked them down.

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.280
Melos ran like the black wind.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:15.540
He ran straight through the middle of a field where a feast was being held.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.460
He kicked away dogs, jumped over small rivers.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:23.920
He ran ten times faster than the sun that sunk little by little.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:26.880
Ah, Melos!

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.470
My name is Philostratos!

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:33.600
I am an apprentice of your friend Selinuntius!

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.470
It's hopeless now!

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:36.480
It's no use!

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:38.350
Stop trying to go there!

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.310
You cannot save him anymore!

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.520
No, the sun has not sunk yet.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.610
He is about to get executed right now!

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.450
You are too late!

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:50.610
I am in despair!

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:54.450
If only you came just a bit earlier!

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:58.040
No, the sun has not sunk yet.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:37.870
Did you manage to write it?

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.120
That "Run, Melos!" thing.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:56.850
Traitor!

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:58.720
Don't you know?

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.060
I've been waiting!

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.640
I've always been...

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.190
Always since that day...

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.310
Always...

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:09.360
I believed that if I just kept writing...

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:12.570
Someday, I would meet you...

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:22.250
Do you know how I've felt these past 15 years while I waited for you?!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:25.460
Do you know?

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:34.970
Sorry.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.020
Hey.

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.020
Won't you let me hear it?

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:45.980
The ending of Melos.

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:49.610
It's trash.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:52.490
It's not something I would tell to you.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:53.610
I want to hear it.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:16:59.280
Melos...

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.040
Melos was both physically and mentally exhausted

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:07.790
and had given up on going to Selinuntius for a moment.

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:10.500
But he changed his mind.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.760
Because there was someone who
trusted him and was waiting for him.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:18.720
Because there was someone waiting for him who entrusted him with his life.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:21.430
Melos drew on his last remaining willpower

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.100
and ran to the royal castle.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.270
And then...

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:31.480
It's sunset.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:34.820
It's a pity, citizens.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.950
I am so disappointed.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:41.160
This man trusted his friend and became his substitute.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:45.000
I too foolishly believed those words.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.670
This man is innocent.

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:49.710
However, the promise must be fulfilled.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:51.920
On with his punishment!

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:58.510
Wait!

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.010
Wait...

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:04.180
That man must not be killed!

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.560
Melos has come back!

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:08.400
Just as promised!

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:10.520
Melos is back now!

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.650
It's me, executioner!

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.280
I'm the one who is to be killed!

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.360
Melos!

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:19.950
I, who made him a hostage, am here!

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:55.900
My husband has had a chronic heart disease since birth.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:59.360
His father died of the same illness.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:02.370
As I heard, when he was still a
student and his father was still alive,

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:04.120
he said he wanted to go to Tokyo,

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:07.750
and had a quarrel with his father.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:11.630
I see.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.250
I did not know this.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:17.130
Don't you find words curious?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:23.510
You suddenly remember them,
even when you have long forgotten them,

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:27.560
and they either hurt you or cheer you up.

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:37.400
Thank you, Mister Takada.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:39.320
Ah, it's nothing.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.280
Come on.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.290
Here.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:50.870
I wonder what this is.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:14.020
Could you accept this as a memento?

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:19.440
I tried to give it to our child as a toy since it's broken,

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:21.820
but my husband got very angry.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.820
When I asked him about it,

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:27.490
he said this watch was yours.

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:42.550
I see.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.760
So that's what Joshima said.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:54.940
Thank you.

00:20:56.520 --> 00:21:00.150
I've been looking for it... for a very, very long time.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:08.950
May 1950

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:11.790
Is it more painful to wait?

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:14.870
Or to keep someone waiting?

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.330
In any case,

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:21.300
there was no need to wait anymore.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:25.010
That was the most painful thing.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:29.510
Yes?

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.510
Takada!

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:34.680
I was worried since I couldn't get in touch with you.

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:38.060
So how is the manuscript coming along?

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:39.980
It's done.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.400
Just as planned.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:44.030
Really? Great!

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:45.740
I knew you could do it!

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.870
I'll tell the others here that you're done.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.330
Thank you!

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:59.040
Actually, Takada, I have another job for you.

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:18.350
What's the job?

00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:20.900
Run, Melos!

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:24.980
End
Run, Melos!

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:30.010
The Spider's Thread
Next Time
